## Interface: 120100
## Title: Ka0s Absorb Tracker
## Notes: Display your total absorb shield value in a clean, customizable bar interface.
## Author: add1kted2ka0s
## Version: 1.11.0
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\AbsorbTracker\media\logos\absorbtracker.logo.128.tga
## SavedVariables: AbsorbTrackerDB, AbsorbTrackerPerfDB
## OptionalDeps: Ace3, LibStub, CallbackHandler-1.0, LibSharedMedia-3.0, LibDataBroker-1.1, LibDBIcon-1.0
## DefaultState: enabled
## Category-enUS: Combat
## X-License: MIT
## X-Standard: https://github.com/tusharsaxena/WowAddonStandards
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1450165

# Libraries (vendored in libs/ — load first)
#@no-lib-strip@
libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
libs\CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.xml
libs\AceAddon-3.0\AceAddon-3.0.xml
libs\AceEvent-3.0\AceEvent-3.0.xml
libs\AceTimer-3.0\AceTimer-3.0.xml
libs\AceConsole-3.0\AceConsole-3.0.xml
libs\AceDB-3.0\AceDB-3.0.xml
libs\AceGUI-3.0\AceGUI-3.0.xml
libs\AceConfig-3.0\AceConfig-3.0.xml
libs\AceDBOptions-3.0\AceDBOptions-3.0.xml
libs\LibDataBroker-1.1\LibDataBroker-1.1.lua
libs\LibDBIcon-1.0\LibDBIcon-1.0.lua
libs\LibKa0s\LibKa0s.xml
libs\LibSharedMedia-3.0\lib.xml
libs\AceGUI-3.0-SharedMediaWidgets\widget.xml
#@end-no-lib-strip@

# Locales
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.L, read at file load by core/DebugLogSetup.lua (the DebugLog descriptor), modules/Bar.lua and settings/Slash.lua (the NS.COMMANDS rows).
locales\enUS.lua

# Core (the LibKa0s-Env seam loads first)
# The LibKa0s-Env seam: this addon reads its own TOC manifest through it. Nothing here is resolved
# at load, so this position is conventional rather than load-bearing.
core\EnvSetup.lua
# Before Constants, deliberately: Constants.FONT_MONO is resolved from the NS.MediaFont seam
# this file publishes, so a Constants that loaded first would resolve it to the fallback.
core\MediaSetup.lua
core\Constants.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.version, captured into the perf descriptor by core/PerfSetup.lua at file load.
core\Namespace.lua
# Conventional order, not load-bearing: State.lua here, and Data.lua and Database.lua below, publish
# tables and functions nothing captures at file load; every reader resolves them at call time.
core\State.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.NewBusTarget / NS.MSG; core/AbsorbTracker.lua subscribes UNITS with them at file load behind a guard, so a later position fails silently.
core\Bus.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.Print / NS.Util.print and NS.LIBKA0S_MISSING, captured at file load by LauncherSetup, AbsorbTracker and the stub branches of DebugLogSetup and PerfSetup.
core\CoreSetup.lua
# The stand-down latch. BEFORE PerfSetup, and that is load-bearing rather than tidy: Perf 12
# requires `descriptor.lifecycle` and refuses at New without it, so a PerfSetup that loaded first
# would raise. It is also where `enabled` and the perf arm stop being two mechanisms.
core\Lifecycle.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.Perf, a file-scope upvalue in core/AbsorbTracker.lua, modules/Display.lua and modules/Timer.lua (performance-§1).
core\PerfSetup.lua
core\Data.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.Units, whose DeepCopy core/Database.lua takes at file load.
core\Units.lua
core\Database.lua
core\DebugLogSetup.lua
# The launcher seam. Builds the object at load and publishes NS.Launcher; the Register() that
# hands it to LibDataBroker and LibDBIcon waits for OnInitialize, because db.global.minimap does
# not exist until NS:InitDB has run.
core\LauncherSetup.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.Widgets, captured as a file-scope upvalue by modules/Bar.lua and modules/Display.lua.
core\WidgetsSetup.lua
core\AbsorbTracker.lua

# Defaults
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.defaults, NS.flatDefaults and NS.unitDefaults; modules/Bar.lua, settings/General.lua and settings/Appearance.lua capture them at file load, and Bar sizes its three frames from them there.
defaults\Profile.lua

# Modules
# Conventional order, not load-bearing: Bar, Display and Timer capture only core seams at file load;
# what they publish to each other (NS.bars, NS.ForEachUnit, NS.RequestRepaint) is resolved at call time.
modules\Bar.lua
modules\Display.lua
modules\Timer.lua
# The diagnostics report's sections (debug-logging-§14). After every module whose state it reads;
# nothing reads it at file load, since the DebugLog descriptor asks for the list when a report runs.
modules\Diagnostics.lua

# Settings (last — depend on everything else being initialized)
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.SchemaRuntime (AllRows/BulkBegin/BulkEnd, read at file load by settings/OptionsSetup.lua; FindRow by settings/Slash.lua) and NS.RegisterSchemaRows (called at file load by settings/General.lua and settings/Appearance.lua).
settings\Schema.lua
# Conventional order, not load-bearing: NS.Slash and NS.COMMANDS are read at call time (OnInitialize, the About page render).
settings\Slash.lua
# LOAD-BEARING: publishes NS.Helpers, captured as a file-scope upvalue by settings/UnitPanel.lua, About.lua, General.lua and Appearance.lua and called inside NS.RegisterSchemaRows at load; and NS.RegisterOptionsPage, called at file load behind a guard (a later position fails silently) by General.lua, Appearance.lua and Profiles.lua.
settings\OptionsSetup.lua
# Conventional order, not load-bearing: UnitPanel and About add functions to NS.Helpers that are called at render time.
settings\UnitPanel.lua
settings\About.lua
settings\General.lua
settings\Appearance.lua
# Conventional order, not load-bearing: last only by habit; nothing reads what it registers until the panel opens.
settings\Profiles.lua
